    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a prime matchup against Quantrill, leveraging an elite .469 xwOBA and a favorable batting order spot to anchor the lineup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a top priority despite a 35% rain risk; his efficiency is bolstered significantly by a 14% platoon edge against Greene and a premium leadoff spot. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Trea Turner** (68.35) and **Junior Caminero** (67.34), both of whom offer elite production potential against Flaherty and Castillo, respectively, provided they navigate their individual SP-skill hurdles.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes efficiency over raw power, leading to a difficult bench decision for **Carson Benge** (47.06). While **Carson Benge** presented a viable floor, he was edged out by **Luke Raley** (54.62) and **Casey Schmitt** (53.08) due to their superior platoon leverage and situational sprint-speed advantages, which we continue to over-weight in our 5x5 framework. **Caleb Durbin** also fell just short of the cut at 46.32; his exclusion was largely driven by a unfavorable -12% SP skill modifier against McLean and the lack of confirmed lineup placement. Managers should monitor **Christian Yelich** (53.55) closely; while his platoon advantage against Ashcraft is strong (+13%), his low score is suppressed by a severe -19% SP skill penalty, making him a candidate to underperform if he fails to capitalize on early-count opportunities.",
